cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use StateSync-GKR in research, please cite this repository."
title: "StateSync-GKR"
abstract: >-
  StateSync-GKR is a Rust prover component that proves sparse-Merkle state
  transitions with a layered GKR protocol, compiling membership,
  non-membership, and single-leaf update operations into a layered arithmetic
  circuit and reducing that circuit through sumcheck. The operation semantics,
  the verification-circuit compiler, the layer reduction, and their
  composition are mechanized in Isabelle/HOL across six registered sessions
  that build with no admitted proof, and the Rust implementation is connected
  to those models through
  recorded contracts, differential tests, and adversarial vectors.
  Version 1.1.1 revises distribution licensing and package metadata. The
  historical v1.1 executable and proof retain their recorded scope; an exact
  compiled identity has not been established for the current metadata source.
type: software
version: "1.1.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23280552"
